# mergeCraft image vulnerability waivers (D7)
#
# Every entry below a CVE id must include, in the preceding comment block:
#   justification: <why the finding is accepted and what mitigates it>
#   expiry: YYYY-MM-DD  (waivers must be renewed or removed before this date)
#
# CI runs scripts/check_trivyignore_expiry.py in sbom-scan and fails on expired
# entries. See docs/supply-chain.md for the operator workflow.
#
# Baseline: operator must record HIGH/CRITICAL findings on the current pre-0.0.1
# image before the blocking gate ships; add dated entries here or fix upstream.

# justification: CVE-2026-78661 is in golang.org/x/net v0.60.0 (fixed 0.62.0)
#   inside the bundled gh CLI. The Action uses gh only for trusted GitHub API
#   output, not for rendering attacker-supplied HTML. Upstream check on
#   2026-11-08: cli/cli v2.103.3 and trunk still resolve x/net v0.61.0, so
#   there is no verified upstream source to pin with the v0.62.0 fix yet.
#   Retain this time-boxed waiver until both images rebuild from fixed upstream
#   and unwaived Trivy JSON/SARIF confirm this CVE is absent.
# expiry: 2026-12-15
CVE-2026-78661
